---
import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Testimonial from '../components/Testimonial.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Authentic Approach | Marcus Levine"
	description="A 3-month 1:1 coaching container: learn to calmly and confidently approach people you're attracted to - and express your interest in them respectfully, yet directly."
>
	<div class="stack gap-20">
		<main class="wrapper stack gap-15 offer">
			<Hero
				title="Authentic Approach"
				tagline="A 3-month 1:1 coaching container: learn to calmly and confidently approach people you're attracted to - and express your interest in them respectfully, yet directly."
			>
				<div class="hero-cta">
					<CallToAction href="https://cal.com/marcuslevine/discovery">
						Book a free discovery call
						<Icon icon="calendar" size="1.2em" />
					</CallToAction>
					<p class="cta-note">30 minutes, real talk about your love life. If this isn't your next step, I'll tell you so.</p>
				</div>
			</Hero>

			<img
				class="offer-img"
				src="/assets/smiling-lean-hat.jpg"
				alt="Marcus looking calm and confident"
				width="960"
				height="640"
			/>

			<section class="content stack gap-4">
				<p class="pull-quote">
					<span class="accent">So you met someone cute at a party.</span> 
					Did you talk to her - or rehearse the perfect opener until she left?
				</p>
				<p>
					If that sounds familiar, you're in the right place. I coach single men who want real
					connection but struggle to actually approach.
				</p>
				<p>
					<span class="accent">Rejection</span> feels unbearable.<br />
					You worry about coming off as <span class="accent">creepy</span>.
				</p>
				<p>I get it, because I've been there.</p>
				<p class="fine">
					(I work primarily with men who date women - but the door is open to anyone who wants
					to approach the people they're attracted to, whatever your gender or orientation.)
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="content stack gap-4">
				<h2>Why "just be confident" has never worked for you</h2>
				<p>
					Freezing isn't cowardice. It's your nervous system tagging rejection as a threat -
					sending you into fight, flight, freeze, or fawn - and doing its job very well. You can't think your way
					out of a body response. No amount of advice, videos, or rehearsed openers will fix it,
					because approach anxiety, and the fear of being creepy, aren't information problems.
					They're body problems.
				</p>
				<p>
					So we train the body. Somatic tools to settle the threat response. Weekly real-world reps,
					with gradually increasing stakes so your body can handle it. And a coach in your corner for the
					scary moments.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="content stack gap-4">
				<h2>Who this is for</h2>
				<p>
					You want to connect with people you're attracted to. You're tired of overthinking every
					interaction. You don't want tricks. You want to become someone for whom talking to
					people you're drawn to is just a normal part of the week.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Who it's not for:</strong> guys looking for manipulation tactics, scripts to
					"win" women, or a coach who'll promise you a girlfriend by week six. I'm NOT training
					pick-up artists.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="content stack gap-4">
				<h2>The promise</h2>
				<p>Three months from now, you:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Approach regularly.</strong> Talking to people you're drawn to is a normal
						part of your week, not a once-a-year act of courage.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Handle rejection without spiraling.</strong> A "no" stings for a minute, not
						a month. You know your worth doesn't ride on any single interaction.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Know what you want, and voice it.</strong> You're clear on what you're
						looking for, and you can express it without apology or pressure.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					I can't promise outcomes with any particular person. What I promise
					is structured training: exercises to rep, support when you need it, and honest feedback,
					every week.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="content stack gap-4">
				<h2>What you get</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>An extended onboarding deep-dive (2.5 to 3 hours)</strong> - your story, your
						goals, your fears, mapped in one unhurried session.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>12 weekly 1:1 sessions</strong> (60 min, video) - a somatic check-in, a
						review of your week's reps, and new concepts to work with.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Weekly field challenges</strong> - real-world reps, scaled to where you are.
						Week one might be eye contact with yourself in the mirror, or smiling at strangers.
						Later on, it might be collecting five rejections on purpose - and thanking every one.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Between-session support</strong> - voice note and text access, for the moment
						right after a hard rejection or when you're struggling to get motivated.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Personalized practices</strong> - self-compassion and nervous-system tools
						so your confidence lives in your body, not just your head.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Frameworks that stick</strong> - clear ways to figure out what you actually
						want, consent practiced as a skill, and a grounded picture of how women experience
						being approached - informed by real stories from women.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="banner">
				<p>"Rejection is <span>information</span>, not failure."</p>
			</section>

			<section class="content stack gap-4">
				<h2>Investment</h2>
				<p>
					<strong>3-month container - $2,220</strong> (paid in full), or
					<strong> 3 payments of $800</strong>.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="guarantee">
				<h2>If the work doesn't move you, your money back</h2>
				<p>
					In week one we take two baselines: two short questionnaires researchers use to track social anxiety and fear of being judged (the SIAS and BFNE-S, if you like acronyms), plus a simple count of how many people you approach each week. We take them again at week eight and week twelve.
				</p>
				<p>
					Show up to <b>every session</b>, do <b>every weekly challenge</b>, and keep your journal for all twelve weeks. If by the end <b>neither your scores nor your weekly approach count has moved</b>, I <b>refund you in full</b>.
				</p>
				<p class="guarantee-fine">
					This isn't a promise about any particular woman. Nobody honest can make that one. It's a promise about the training: if you do it and it doesn't move you, you don't pay for it.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="content stack gap-4">
				<h2>From people I've coached</h2>
				<Testimonial name="Adam L" location="USA">
					<p class="pull-quote">"Marcus' training in direct, honest, and respectful communication has
					been a <span class="accent">transformative experience</span>.</p>
					<p>Now, I have the confidence to approach women and talk to them
					in a natural way, without feeling creepy or awkward. If a woman expresses that they're
					not interested, it is so freeing to receive her 'no' with gratitude and respect - instead of
					feeling rejected or taking it personally.</p>
					<p>This shift has made dating more fun than ever. Even when things don't go in a
					romantic direction, I often end up making new friends and forming meaningful connections based
					in authenticity and genuine mutual interest. Working with Marcus played a huge role in
					relieving my social anxiety and helping me live in the moment - taking action instead of staring
					across the room wondering. I've never felt more alive."
					</p>
				</Testimonial>
				<Testimonial name="Sandra" location="Finland" photo="/assets/sandra.jpg">
					<p class="pull-quote">"Marcus <span class="accent">broadened my perspective</span> on what
					intimacy can be.</p>
					<p>He invited me to explore my deepest desires, opening me up for more pleasure and
					expression. I always felt safe, seen and heard with him, as we unlocked insights into my
					relationship history, dynamics and patterns.</p>
					<p>With greater respect for myself, now I am able to communicate more effectively, voicing
					my desires and boundaries, needs and expectations. After working with Marcus, I feel
					safer and more empowered in my connections."
					</p>
				</Testimonial>
			</section>

			<section class="final-cta stack gap-4">
				<h2>Let's talk</h2>
				<p>
					The first rep is deciding to do the work. If you're ready to date the
					people in the room who you're most attracted to, book a free discovery call.
				</p>
				<div class="hero-cta">
					<CallToAction href="https://cal.com/marcuslevine/discovery">
						Book a free discovery call
						<Icon icon="calendar" size="1.2em" />
					</CallToAction>
					<p class="cta-note">Let's bring back in-person dating!</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.offer {
		padding-top: 2rem;
	}

	.hero-cta {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}

	.cta-note {
		font-size: var(--text-md);
		color: var(--gray-400);
	}

	.offer-img {
		max-height: 30rem;
		width: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
		object-position: center 30%;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
	}

	:global(html.theme-dark) .offer-img {
		box-shadow: 0 12px 28px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
	}

	.content {
		max-width: 65ch;
		margin-inline: auto;
		width: 100%;
		font-size: var(--text-md);
		color: var(--gray-200);
	}

	.content h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-2xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}

	.content ul {
		padding-inline-start: 1.25rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.fine {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--gray-400);
	}

	/* A two-line, two-tone pull quote: bigger serif italic type breaks up the prose rhythm,
	   with .accent picking out a word or phrase in the brand accent color. Reused inside
	   testimonial blockquotes as the "lede" line, and once in body copy as a standalone beat. */
	.pull-quote {
		font-family: var(--font-brand);
		font-style: italic;
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: var(--text-lg);
		line-height: 1.35;
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}

	.pull-quote .accent {
		color: var(--accent-regular);
		font-style: normal;
	}

	@media (min-width: 50em) {
		.pull-quote {
			font-size: var(--text-xl);
		}
	}

	/* Testimonial paragraphs are slotted into Testimonial.astro from here, so its own
	   `.testimonial-content p` rule can't reach them (different scope) - space them here instead. */
	:global(.testimonial-content p) {
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	:global(.testimonial-content p:last-child) {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	.banner {
		background: var(--gray-0);
		color: var(--gray-999);
		text-align: center;
		padding: 3.5rem 1.5rem;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
	}

	.banner p {
		font-family: var(--font-brand);
		font-style: italic;
		font-size: var(--text-2xl);
		color: var(--gray-999);
	}

	.banner span {
		color: var(--accent-light);
	}

	.guarantee {
		background: var(--gray-0);
		border: 2px solid var(--accent-regular);
		border-radius: 1rem;
		padding: 2rem;
		max-width: 65ch;
		margin-inline: auto;
		text-align: center;
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
	}

	:global(html.theme-dark) .guarantee {
		background: var(--gray-800);
		border-color: var(--accent-dark);
	}

	.guarantee h2 {
		color: var(--accent-regular);
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	:global(html.theme-dark) .guarantee h2 {
		color: var(--accent-dark);
	}

	.guarantee p {
		color: var(--gray-900);
		font-size: var(--text-md);
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	:global(html.theme-dark) .guarantee p {
		color: var(--gray-200);
	}

	.guarantee p.guarantee-fine {
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--gray-700);
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	:global(html.theme-dark) .guarantee p.guarantee-fine {
		color: var(--gray-400);
	}

	.final-cta {
		text-align: center;
		align-items: center;
		max-width: 65ch;
		margin-inline: auto;
	}

	.final-cta h2 {
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}

	@media (min-width: 50em) {
		.hero-cta {
			align-items: center;
		}
	}
</style>
